kpi Region | eu-north-1
kpi Farms | 6
kpi Peak load | 18000 msg/s
kpi Uplink buffer | 6 hours | oldest readings dropped after that | bad

## Overview

Turbine readings flow from each farm into one central stream and are processed once. The results are then split into a fast store for dashboards and a cheap archive for audits.

## Pipeline diagram

diagram pipe dir=TB title="Telemetry pipeline, eu-north-1"
pipe: tc "Turbine Controllers" ext
pipe: gw "Edge Gateway" svc
pipe: stream "Telemetry Stream" queue focus
pipe: proc "Stream Processor" fn focus
pipe: ts "Timeseries Store" db
pipe: arch "Raw Archive" store
pipe: alert "Alerting Service" svc
pipe: dash "Operations Dashboard" svc
pipe: tc -> gw : OPC UA, 1 Hz
pipe: gw -> stream : MQTT over TLS, batched every 5 s
pipe: stream -> proc : consumer
pipe: proc -> ts : 10 s aggregates
pipe: proc -> arch : Parquet every 15 minutes
pipe: proc -> alert : threshold breach
pipe: ts -> dash : queries
pipe: group farm "At each farm (on site, outside the cloud account)" tc, gw
pipe: group cloud "Cloud account (eu-north-1)" stream, proc, ts, arch, alert, dash

## Capacity and retention

table = component,size,retention; Telemetry Stream,"24 shards, 18000 messages per second at peak",not stated; Timeseries Store,fast store for dashboards,"7 days in memory, 3 years on magnetic storage"; Raw Archive,cheap archive for audits,"10 years, moved to cold storage after 90 days"

## If the uplink fails

!! The Edge Gateway buffers only 6 hours of readings. After that the oldest readings are dropped for good.

1. The Edge Gateway buffers up to 6 hours of readings on disk.
2. When the link returns, it replays them in order.
3. If the outage lasts longer than 6 hours, the oldest readings are dropped.
